{
  "case_id": "2022-22-148",
  "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Jack Daniel's Properties, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case involves a dog toy that copies Jack Daniel's trademark and trade dress and associates its whiskey with dog poop. After a four-day trial, the district court found both infringement and dilution. The Ninth Circuit erroneously reversed both holdings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Could a statement be -- could it fail Rogers and be misleading yet not be confusing under the Lanham Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Ms. Blatt, I'm -- I'm just wondering why you are making such a broad argument when there are pretty obvious narrower arguments available to you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, by the way, only seven people said they thought there was a confusion as to who owned it -- I mean who needed permission, and that still left 25 percent confusion, which is still, you know, a massively high consumer survey."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I -- I take it your short answer to Justice Sotomayor's hypothetical where, let's say, the -- the survey shows 25 percent -- let's say it shows 30 percent, your answer is that has to go to a jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. BLATT",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "says that Congress shall make no law infringing the freedom of speech. That's a text that takes precedence over the Lanham Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I just want to make sure I understand your position with respect to the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, as -- as applied by the Ninth Circuit, Rogers is an antecedent test that the infringement plaintiff has to satisfy in order to even invoke the Lanham Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I always have hesitation in doing away with something that circuits have been relying on, all -- virtually all of them, but applying it in different contexts. And we have amicus brief from different stakeholders, some saying it may not apply in parody, but it could apply in movie titles, it might apply in something else and not this, in novels, et cetera."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: And, counsel, I'd like to understand what you would have us do with respect to the remand, because you do argue that even under the Lanham Act's text, always a place to start, likelihood of confusion, that the district court erred and it didn't fully account for the parody nature of --of this product."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, it's one piece of the puzzle here, but it's not the whole thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So is your concern -- are you as much concerned about the test itself or the location of the test? So what if your test and the factors that are concerning you are rolled into the multifactor test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Can I ask you, you -- you said that Rogers screens out expressive works, and I think part -- part of the problem that I'm struggling with is all of the uncertainty we have as to whether or not something is sufficiently expressive, and that -- that seems to be where there's a lot of problems in the administrability of the Rogers test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Because I -- maybe I just have no sense of humor, but -- (Laughter.)\nJUSTICE KAGAN: -- what's the parody?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cooper",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COOPER: The -- the parody is multifold. The -- the --the testimony indicates, and it's not been disputed, that the parody is to make fun of marks that take themselves seriously."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cooper",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COOPER. Well, here's the problem, is that, first of all, \"explicitly misleading\" is a way of identifying a mechanism of confusion, so it's consistent with the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, I -- I still don't know what that means, but give me an example of something that is commercial then."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cooper",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COOPER: A commercial would be an advertisement.\nJUSTICE THOMAS: No, no, no.\nSomething that is commercial, that does -- that\nfits -- that it's not noncommercial.\nMR. COOPER: I think an advertisement\nwould be commercial speech, that it proposes a\ntransaction. And so, if we were to have\nsomething that advertised a product, let's say\nBad Spaniels Whiskey, and it was an ad for Bad\nSpaniels Whiskey, that advertisement would be\ncommercial speech. You're proposing a\ntransaction.\nBut that's not what we're doing here.\nWe're not selling a bottle of diluted dog poo,\nwhich is the subject of the parody that they're\ncomplaining about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59ebbc138d52549ad4729c03ac29de6947662bdc29c38d156b159b83a4d7cf7d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59ebbc138d52-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice.\nJustice Alito, all trademarks are\nexpressive. They have speech rights. And every\ntime you infringe them, it's going to implicate\nspeech by definition.\nAnd what the other side and I don't\nhear you guys talking about is the half of\nspeech that no one likes, the pornography and\nthe poison. And it is hard for me to see how\nyou can say that the trademark owner doesn't have\nan interest in something that approaches\ncompelled speech if their mark has been using in\nporn films and porn toys and sex toys and people\nare profiting off of that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-22-148",
      "confidence": 0.0,
